WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.561
If my account grows from $1,000 to $1,200,

2
00:00:03.561 --> 00:00:05.256
dips back to $1,000,

3
00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:07.460
and climbs back to $1,200,

4
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.834
do I share 10% and 3% twice?

5
00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:10.343
Never.

6
00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:17.718
Your personal High-Water Mark stays pinned at $1,200—like a pencil mark on a doorframe.

7
00:00:17.718 --> 00:00:23.314
Every recovery dollar from $1,000 back to $1,200 stays 100% yours.

8
00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:27.383
Sharing only resumes on dollar $1,201 and above.

9
00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:34.419
A High-Water Mark protects you from paying a volatility tax during bumpy stretches,

10
00:00:34.419 --> 00:00:40.608
though it does not insure against market losses while a position is open.
